## Heat, Soaking, And Controlled Processing

### δίπλωμα (diploma)
<a id="term-double-vessel"></a>

Meaning: A δίπλωμα is the doubled heating arrangement used when delicate oils, waxes, or perfumes must be warmed gently.

Why it matters: This is the clearest sign that ancient perfume work distinguished between direct fire and protected, indirect heat.

Reader: [full context in tools-texts.md](./tools-texts.md#term-double-vessel)
Index: [lookup entry](./tools-index.md#term-double-vessel)
Citations: 1

Safe claims:
- Used for gentle heating rather than open direct contact with the flame.
- Appears in recipes for melting wax and warming delicate perfume materials.
- Belongs to the same doubled-heating tool family as the explicitly described double vessel.

Do not infer:
- Do not infer a single fixed shape from the shorthand term alone.
- Do not infer that every use involved identical materials or dimensions.

