### κυρτίς (kyrtis)
<a id="term-kyrtis"></a>

Meaning: A κυρτίς is the wicker pressing basket through which oil is squeezed and strained.

Why it matters: It helps separate the basket that holds material under pressure from the press that applies force and from the cloth that merely covers or breathes.

Reader: [full context in tools-texts.md](./tools-texts.md#term-kyrtis)
Index: [lookup entry](./tools-index.md#term-kyrtis)
Citations: 2

Safe claims:
- A κυρτίς is a woven basket used as a pressing filter or strainer.
- It appears with floral oils and with seed-oil extraction.
- In one passage it works together with a screw-press.

Do not infer:
- Do not collapse it into a plain cloth bag.
- Do not infer that every basket of this kind was built or used identically.

### ὄργανον (organon)
<a id="term-organon"></a>

Meaning: In the perfume passage, ὄργανον is the unnamed extraction apparatus through which bruised myrrh is pressed.

Why it matters: This term marks the device that applies extraction pressure, which is exactly the distinction needed to separate press, basket, and cloth in WP7.

Reader: [full context in tools-texts.md](./tools-texts.md#term-organon)
Index: [lookup entry](./tools-index.md#term-organon)
Citations: 1

Safe claims:
- In the perfume passage, ὄργανον is the device through which bruised myrrh is squeezed.
- The term names the apparatus that performs extraction, not the aromatic being processed.
- It belongs with pressing and extraction language rather than with cloth-cover or storage terms.

Do not infer:
- Do not infer the exact construction of the apparatus from the perfume passage alone.
