## Grinding, Stirring, And Mixing

### ὅλμος (holmos)
<a id="term-holmos"></a>

Meaning: A ὅλμος is the heavy mortar in which aromatics are chopped, ground, and worked into the mixture.

Why it matters: This is the clearest mortar term in the perfume corpus and gives the workshop a real working surface, not just vessels and filters.

Reader: [full context in tools-texts.md](./tools-texts.md#term-holmos)
Index: [lookup entry](./tools-index.md#term-holmos)
Citations: 3

Safe claims:
- A ὅλμος is a heavy mortar used to work ingredients together.
- In perfume recipes it is used to grind or incorporate aromatics like myrrh.

Do not infer:
- Do not generalize from the Hippocratic support-use to the perfume-core sense.
- Do not confuse it with the pestle or spatula.

