## Covers, Seals, Insulation, And Handling

### ψίαθος ἀραιά (psiathos araia)
<a id="term-psiathos-araia"></a>

Meaning: Ψίαθος ἀραιά is the loose mat used to cover or separate material without sealing it tight.

Why it matters: WP7 needs this term because ancient perfume work often protected mixtures with porous covers rather than airtight closures.

Reader: [full context in tools-texts.md](./tools-texts.md#term-psiathos-araia)
Index: [lookup entry](./tools-index.md#term-psiathos-araia)
Citations: 1

Safe claims:
- Used as a porous barrier or cover.
- Allows vapor or aroma to move while keeping solids apart.

Do not infer:
- Do not treat it as a press.
- Do not treat it as a hermetic seal.

