### πηλός (pelos)
<a id="term-pelos"></a>

Meaning: Πηλός is the clay lute used to seal a vessel or vessel-joint tightly all the way around.

Why it matters: It lets WP7 explain that ancient perfume work used more than one closure regime: breathable cloth, tied lid, and clay-sealed apparatus.

Reader: [full context in tools-texts.md](./tools-texts.md#term-pelos)
Index: [lookup entry](./tools-index.md#term-pelos)
Citations: 1

Safe claims:
- Used as clay sealant around a vessel.
- Creates a tight closure in a distillation or fumigation setup.

Do not infer:
