## Trade, Shops, And Perfume Professions

### μυρεψική
<a id="term-myrepsike"></a>

Meaning: Μυρεψική is perfumery understood as a craft or trade, not just a vague art of nice smells.

Why it matters: WP7 needs a term for the craft itself if the workshop post is going to describe an actual trade rather than a generic room of vessels.

Reader: [full context in tools-texts.md](./tools-texts.md#term-myrepsike)
Index: [lookup entry](./tools-index.md#term-myrepsike)
Citations: 1

Safe claims:
- Names the craft or trade of perfume-making.
- Can describe a profession one sets up and finances.

Do not infer:
- Do not treat it as a shop-building term by itself.
- Do not collapse the craft into retail alone.

### μυρεψός
<a id="term-myrepsos"></a>

Meaning: Μυρεψός is the perfumer as maker and compounder, not simply the man behind the counter.

Why it matters: This is one of the clearest ways the corpus distinguishes the perfumer from the perfume-seller.

Reader: [full context in tools-texts.md](./tools-texts.md#term-myrepsos)
Index: [lookup entry](./tools-index.md#term-myrepsos)
Citations: 2

Safe claims:
- A μυρεψός is a perfumer or compounder of perfumes.
- The term can be distinguished from the perfume-seller.

Do not infer:
- Do not equate the term automatically with a retailer.
- Do not infer a single legal or social status from all occurrences.

### μυροποιός
<a id="term-myropoios"></a>

Meaning: Μυροποιός is another name for the maker of perfumes.

Why it matters: It confirms that the corpus distinguishes maker-language from seller-language in more than one way.

